ownerT -- NO GRAMMAR RULE GAINS A CHILD FROM AN ACTION BODY (SEQ 214, 2026-09-27).

On the new road an action's body is compiled by a DRIVE of BlocK's generated parse, and the NamE
action gives every name the body mentions an OWNER. aCTionNamE took that owner from currentMETHOD --
and inside a generated body parseRule has set currentMETHOD to the rule it is parsing, so the names
landed in the GRAMMAR: under ANYtoken and, through its shared list, under the six rules that use it as
a term. The next top-level statement that read such a name tried the stray child as a TERM and the
file was abandoned (SEQ 213).

grammarHolds(name) walks the Grokking registry and each rule's terms and prints every holder plus a
count, unconditionally. owAct's body names owX (declared, read), owY (declared, assigned) and owZ
(undeclared -- a new local); the scans run INSIDE owAct, after its own compile, because a polluted
grammar breaks the parse of any later top-level name. The count before parser() is the zero control.
H7, measured on the pre-fix branch build: each of the three reads 7 -- ANYtoken plus six holders.
